Called the ''Garguile'' by the French people, the Gar-Ghoul terrorized France until its Amulet was hidden in [[Rouen]] in the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]], guarded by a giant [[Gargoyle]] statue. Many stone statues were built in its likeness around France and on the [[Cathedral of Notre Dame]] to ward off evil spirits. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}}

Centuries later, Gar-Ghoul began to awaken, its powers causing mysterious waterspouts and whirlpools to occur on the [[Seine River]], capsizing boats and almost drowning people. Both the [[Huntik Foundation]] and [[the Organization]] began searching for the Titan, leading them to the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]] where the two sides fought. Using the battle as a distraction, [[DeFoe]] managed to obtain Gar-Ghoul's [[Amulet]] in and invoked it in battle against [[Dante Vale]]. However, Gar-Ghoul was defeated by [[Caliban]] and called back to its Amulet by DeFoe who fled. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}}.

In the [[Abandoned church in Paris]], DeFoe summoned Gar-Ghoul to fight against Dante's Caliban once more, but althoughGar-Ghoul still could not beat Caliban in battle, the two fought on a more even footing. {{source|Crawling the Catacombs}}

Gar-Ghoul was used by DeFoe alongside [[Kreutalk]] at [[King Basilisk]]'s resting place to battle against the Huntik team for King Basilisk's amulet. Kreutalk severely weakened [[Sabriel]] and [[Freelancer]], making room for Gar-Ghoul to take out Freelancer and presumably also Sabriel. DeFoe made Gar-Ghoul go back to its amulet when Zhalia Moon managed to invoke the powerful King Basilisk. {{source|Absent Heroes}}

Inside one of the Argonaut's ship, DeFoe summoned Gar-Ghoul alongside [[Mindrone]]. Gar-Ghoul fought against Dante and his [[Solwing]] Titan but was defeated by Dante, who used [[Dragonfist]] to knock Gar-Ghoul into a hole in the ship. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

After DeFoe was removed from [[the Organization]], [[Zhalia Moon]] took ownership of Gar-Ghoul, although she did not reveal this action until the final battle against [[the Professor]]. In that battle, it brought [[Nordrake]] out of the air and distracted [[Tao]] for a while until being defeated alongside [[Ariel]] {{source|The Mission}}. 

Zhalia invoked Gar-Ghoul to fight alongside Dante's [[Elf King Oberon]] against [[Wilder]] and his team. Gar-Ghoul was defeated by [[Myrmidon]] after being hit by a [[Weakenshade]] spell cast by Wilder. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Zhalia used Gar-Ghoul again when the Huntik team faced [[Lucas Casterwill]], [[Lane]] and [[Dellix]] at a [[Casterwill Library]]. {{source|Chasing Void}}
